{
  "id": "albanian_kenge_qytetare",
  "name": "Këngë qytetare (Albanian urban song of Shkodër and Elbasan)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Urban song of the old Ottoman-era towns of Albania, above all Shkodër in the north and Elbasan and Berat in the centre, sung at domestic and festive gatherings (aheng) on themes of love and town life. A solo singer is accompanied by a small saze ensemble of violin, clarinet, accordion and def frame drum, in melismatic, makam-inflected melodies; Radio Tirana recorded and broadcast the repertoire from the mid-twentieth century. The dayereh card stands in for the def (dajre) jingled frame drum.",
  "recipe": "classic Eastern European early-1940s këngë qytetare, ballad Poetry, Mediterranean ballad branch. many notes per syllable, solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. fiddle, clarinet, accordion, dense dance driving dayereh. treated studio. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, vari-mu, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
